course: dictionary
lesson: 5955
title: Match: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. Match is a good example. «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» Goal, penalty and dived tell you that a match here is a game between two teams.
explain: Match can also mean a small stick that makes a flame when you strike it. Matches are only for adults, so never play with them or fire. If a sentence talks about a flame, the meaning is the stick, not the game.
explain: Match can be a verb too. To match is to go well together or be the same. «The sitar has sympathetic strings that nobody plucks; they vibrate by themselves when matching notes are played.» Here the matching notes are the same notes, so the strings respond to them. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: A match can be a game between two players or teams, like a football match.
fact: A match can also be a small stick that makes a flame when you strike it.
fact: To match means to go well together or be the same, like matching socks.
fact: To match things means to find pairs that belong together.
fact: To be a match for someone means to be as good as them.
exercise: «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» What kind of match is this? | Two socks that go well together | A small stick that makes a flame | *A game between two teams | A pair of numbers that add up
exercise: Mia must match each sock to its pair. What does match mean here? | *To find pairs that belong together | To play a game against a friend | To strike a flame | To be taller than her friend
exercise: «The sitar has sympathetic strings that nobody plucks; they vibrate by themselves when matching notes are played.» What does matching mean here? | Lost and far away | A game between two teams | *The same, or going well together | A small stick for a flame
test: «Dad is a match for the coach at chess.» What does a match for someone mean? | Lost to the coach at chess | Taller than the coach | *As good as the coach | A game that the coach plays
test: Maths: «We won 3 matches, lost 1 and drew 2, so we played 6 matches.» What does matches mean in this sentence? | *Games played between teams | Pairs of numbers that add up | Matchsticks used to make a shape | Socks that match
exam: Which sentence uses match to mean go well together? | *«The socks match perfectly.» | «The match was won by the home team.» | «Strike the match carefully.»
